From: automation-platform-controller stewardship
Subject: [PATCH] controller: list job templates granted through Execute

Implements: CTL-024 (lab-content AAP-PLATFORM-DEFECTS F180)

The job-template list filtered only on view_jobtemplate. JobTemplate Execute is
defined to include view, but persisted RoleEvaluation data can retain the execute
partial without the implied view partial after managed-role synchronization. In
that state a delegate can execute a template by ID but the template list is empty.

Treat execute_jobtemplate itself as sufficient list visibility. This preserves
least privilege: Execute still grants neither change nor delete, and templates
without either view or execute remain hidden.

Tested by the endpoint regression below, which exercises a team member with the
managed Execute assignment, removes the cached implied-view partial to reproduce
the observed persisted state, and verifies that only the executable template is
listed.
---
diff --git a/awx/main/access.py b/awx/main/access.py
--- a/awx/main/access.py
+++ b/awx/main/access.py
@@ -1477,6 +1477,12 @@ class JobTemplateAccess(NotificationAttachMixin, UnifiedCredentialsMixin, BaseAc
         Prefetch('last_job', queryset=UnifiedJob.objects.non_polymorphic()),
     )

+    def filtered_queryset(self):
+        # Execute is a read-like permission for launchable templates. Query it
+        # explicitly so a stale implied-view evaluation cannot hide a template
+        # that the user is authorized to launch.
+        return (self.model.access_qs(self.user, 'view') | self.model.access_qs(self.user, 'execute')).distinct()
+
